		{
			"id": 1785838,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808/111999483679488382",
			"author": {
				"name": "Curtis Wilcox",
				"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/29c7cdc14a2585bc23ea9dd2241cdd02ca5e676c99928e0f4777682f6cd3e497.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-02-26T19:41:36.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@mikeneu\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>mikeneu</span></a></span> <br />Neat! I think it could benefit from a toggle to make it a static transcript, without the interactivity, so people can read it without the timecodes or button semantics while using a screen reader or any text-to-speech tech.</p><p>The toggle control could do something like add/remove a 'static' class on the custom element and make the click handler inactive.</p><p>```CSS<br />youtube-deep-link.static [data-offset] button {<br />    display: none;<br />}<br />```</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1785837,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808/111999485155714408",
			"author": {
				"name": "Curtis Wilcox",
				"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/29c7cdc14a2585bc23ea9dd2241cdd02ca5e676c99928e0f4777682f6cd3e497.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-02-26T19:41:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@mikeneu\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>mikeneu</span></a></span> <br />Also, the spans have `role=\"button\"` but shouldn't.<br />`&lt;span data-offset=\"0\" role=\"button\"&gt;&lt;button type=\"button\"&gt;00:00&lt;/button&gt;All right, what's up everybody?&lt;/span&gt;`</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		}
	],
